90
00:02:19,334 --> 00:02:20,634
You seem tired.

91
00:02:22,044 --> 00:02:24,464
Oh, Krulcifer.

92
00:02:24,464 --> 00:02:29,794
Thank you for accepting 
Lord Balzeride's challenge yesterday.

93
00:02:29,794 --> 00:02:31,144
I appreciate it.

94
00:02:31,144 --> 00:02:34,684
No problem, but should you really have taken that up?

95
00:02:34,684 --> 00:02:36,594
We only have two days to prepare.

96
00:02:36,594 --> 00:02:37,614
That's true.

97
00:02:37,614 --> 00:02:41,624
Although I put on a tough front,
 our victory is by no means certain.

98
00:02:41,624 --> 00:02:45,654
It would've been a different matter if you could use a Divine Raiment Machine Dragon.

99
00:02:47,294 --> 00:02:49,454
You're taking this pretty well.

100
00:02:50,034 --> 00:02:53,814
A regular person would be pretty annoyed
 to get dragged into a duel like this.

101
00:02:53,814 --> 00:02:56,044
Especially considering we aren't real lovers.

102
00:02:56,044 --> 00:02:59,364
I accepted it of my own free will.

103
00:02:59,364 --> 00:03:00,424
Ah.

104
00:03:00,814 --> 00:03:03,304
So you two aren't real lovers?

105
00:03:03,794 --> 00:03:10,444
Basically, Krulcifer wanted to avoid a political marriage, so she had you act as her boyfriend.

106
00:03:10,444 --> 00:03:12,054
That's about it, right?

107
00:03:12,054 --> 00:03:14,264
That's a load off my mind.

108
00:03:14,264 --> 00:03:15,954
Uh, well...

109
00:03:15,954 --> 00:03:20,564
That duel should be a piece of cake,
 given how skilled the both of you are.

110
00:03:21,234 --> 00:03:22,654
I hope you're right.

111
00:03:24,064 --> 00:03:29,154
All right! Then I'll go do some
 upgrades on Lux's Mechanical Dragon.

112
00:03:29,154 --> 00:03:32,064
I should do something to
 enhance its attack capabilities.

113
00:03:32,064 --> 00:03:34,324
I know! I'll attach a drill!

114
00:03:34,324 --> 00:03:36,204
Uh, I'm not sure that's the best idea.

115
00:03:36,204 --> 00:03:39,474
Lux, let's pass on a date today.

116
00:03:39,474 --> 00:03:40,844
I have something to take care of.

117
00:03:40,844 --> 00:03:41,834
Bye.

118
00:03:42,214 --> 00:03:43,524
Oh, okay. Bye.

119
00:03:43,524 --> 00:03:46,964
I'm pretty sure a drill would come in handy, you know.

120
00:03:49,094 --> 00:03:50,504
Are you tired?

121
00:03:50,504 --> 00:03:55,854
Well, I had some jobs to do early in the morning,
 so I just haven't gotten enough sleep.

122
00:03:57,064 --> 00:03:59,854
I see. That's understandable.

123
00:04:09,564 --> 00:04:10,654
What's this?

124
00:04:10,654 --> 00:04:12,864
Where's your girlfriend today?

125
00:04:13,454 --> 00:04:16,374
I bet you're lonely, Luxy.

126
00:04:16,374 --> 00:04:19,874
Oh, uh... I'm guessing you
 have a job for me, right?

127
00:04:21,034 --> 00:04:23,644
Would you come with me for a bit?

128
00:04:23,644 --> 00:04:25,604
H-Hold on!

129
00:04:27,214 --> 00:04:29,704
Please come right in.

130
00:04:32,264 --> 00:04:35,894
Welcome, Master.

131
00:04:35,894 --> 00:04:37,764
Huh?! Wh-What?!

132
00:04:37,764 --> 00:04:42,184
We're here to soothe the master's
 weariness from a hard day's work.

133
00:04:42,184 --> 00:04:42,914
Huh?!

134
00:04:42,914 --> 00:04:46,264
Relax and enjoy, Master.

135
00:04:46,264 --> 00:04:48,774
Uh, just what in the world is going on?

136
00:04:48,774 --> 00:04:55,524
You see, Master, Miss Lisha
 came to me asking what you'd like.

137
00:04:55,524 --> 00:05:01,044
The princess said she didn't know
 what a young man would find pleasing.

138
00:05:01,044 --> 00:05:03,974
H-Hey! You promised not to say that!

139
00:05:04,664 --> 00:05:09,544
So, imagining what your fond memories of being a prince would be,

140
00:05:09,544 --> 00:05:15,424
I came to the conclusion that you'd like it
 the most if we acted as your maids!

141
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:21,314
But I've never really had maids take care of me.

142
00:05:21,314 --> 00:05:24,464
Then enjoy this new opportunity to its fullest!

143
00:05:24,464 --> 00:05:25,944
Even though we're all amateurs!

144
00:05:26,354 --> 00:05:28,354
Lu, let's eat together.

145
00:05:28,354 --> 00:05:29,894
Uh, but...

146
00:05:29,894 --> 00:05:32,574
Is this too much?

147
00:05:33,204 --> 00:05:35,904
Suddenly springing something like this on you?

148
00:05:35,904 --> 00:05:38,644
Not at all! I'm very flattered, Miss Lisha.

149
00:05:38,644 --> 00:05:39,804
Thank you very much!

150
00:05:40,344 --> 00:05:41,714
Really?!

151
00:05:41,714 --> 00:05:46,964
Th-Then for today, you can
 consider me your personal maid...

152
00:05:47,314 --> 00:05:50,964
and do dirty things to me.

153
00:05:50,964 --> 00:05:52,594
I'm not doing anything like that!

154
00:05:52,594 --> 00:05:54,834
What? Really?

155
00:05:54,834 --> 00:05:59,554
Tillfur told me that's part of a maid's job.

156
00:06:05,224 --> 00:06:08,484
Royal Capitol, Castle Atismata

157
00:06:05,224 --> 00:06:08,484
Royal Capitol, Castle Atismata

158
00:06:08,484 --> 00:06:14,584
How many years has it been since we,
 the Four Great Houses, were last called here?

159
00:06:08,734 --> 00:06:12,734
Assembly Hall

160
00:06:08,734 --> 00:06:12,734
Assembly Hall

161
00:06:14,584 --> 00:06:17,744
Was it not when the new
 kingdom was established?

162
00:06:18,214 --> 00:06:22,044
In any case, the current matter must be of great importance.

163
00:06:22,044 --> 00:06:25,244
I'm certain you all know what a Ragnarok is.

164
00:06:25,634 --> 00:06:29,644
The most powerful of Abysses,
 possessing supernatural powers,

165
00:06:29,644 --> 00:06:32,884
one of which exists in each ruin.

166
00:06:32,884 --> 00:06:34,004
What about them?

167
00:06:34,004 --> 00:06:41,264
Poseidon, the Ragnarok that was once subdued and turned to stone, is beginning to break free.

168
00:06:42,114 --> 00:06:43,064
What?!

169
00:06:43,064 --> 00:06:45,114
Is that certain?!

170
00:06:45,114 --> 00:06:48,984
Essentially, you'd like us to prepare for that.

171
00:06:49,394 --> 00:06:56,154
However, with the current military power of the new kingdom, I'm not sure we can fell a Ragnarok.

172
00:06:56,154 --> 00:06:58,234
What are our options, then?

173
00:06:58,234 --> 00:07:00,054
There is only one thing we can do.

174
00:07:02,794 --> 00:07:04,284
Lord Warg?

175
00:07:04,284 --> 00:07:09,514
In order to defeat the Ragnarok,
 we must investigate the ruins as soon as possible,

176
00:07:09,514 --> 00:07:13,164
and obtain the powerful
 weapons that lie therein.

177
00:07:13,164 --> 00:07:15,464
That is our only hope.

178
00:07:15,464 --> 00:07:19,344
I'd like to entrust my son with that mission.

179
00:07:28,394 --> 00:07:32,694
I've gathered you to talk about tomorrow's investigations of the ruins.

180
00:07:33,194 --> 00:07:37,324
Officially it will be considered 
an ordinary ruins investigations.

181
00:07:37,324 --> 00:07:39,614
However, its true purpose is this.

182
00:07:42,594 --> 00:07:49,894
As I've already told some of you, it's said that
 one needs a key to enter the core of the ruins.

183
00:07:49,894 --> 00:07:54,214
I think it's likely that this horn is that key.

184
00:07:54,214 --> 00:07:55,824
Now, Lux.

185
00:07:55,824 --> 00:07:56,454
Yes, ma'am!

186
00:08:00,054 --> 00:08:02,564
I'm entrusting it to you.

187
00:08:02,564 --> 00:08:03,694
Understood.

188
00:08:07,934 --> 00:08:09,604
That's right, Lux!

189
00:08:09,604 --> 00:08:14,844
I'll upgrade your Machine Dragon,
 so you can do even better in tomorrow's mission.

190
00:08:14,844 --> 00:08:15,914
Maybe a drill wouldâ

191
00:08:15,914 --> 00:08:16,864
No, thanks.

192
00:08:16,864 --> 00:08:18,014
Wh-What?!

193
00:08:18,014 --> 00:08:20,834
Can you not see the charm of the drill?

194
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:25,504
You know, drills are useful in so many ways, and they'll increase your attack potential so much too!

195
00:08:23,414 --> 00:08:24,994
<i>Krulcifer?</i>

196
00:08:25,504 --> 00:08:26,834
<i>What's she doing here?</i>

197
00:08:31,454 --> 00:08:32,624
Krulcifer!

198
00:08:33,934 --> 00:08:35,174
What is it?

199
00:08:35,174 --> 00:08:37,284
Why were you at the meeting?

200
00:08:37,284 --> 00:08:41,094
Because I will be taking part in
 tomorrow's mission. Why else?

201
00:08:41,094 --> 00:08:48,224
But you're a foreign student. You wouldn't normally be allowed to participate in ruins investigations.

202
00:08:48,224 --> 00:08:50,134
I asked to join.

203
00:08:50,134 --> 00:08:53,984
I'd like to ask you to treat me the same
 as everyone else on the team.

204
00:08:53,984 --> 00:08:55,734
But why did you want to join?

205
00:08:56,524 --> 00:09:00,744
It's one of the few precious opportunities I have to fulfill my goal.

206
00:09:01,484 --> 00:09:02,114
Excuse me.

207
00:09:04,484 --> 00:09:05,684
Your goal?

208
00:09:10,464 --> 00:09:12,604
It's been a while.

209
00:09:16,864 --> 00:09:22,004
<i>Still, why did Krulcifer
 join the ruins investigation?</i>

210
00:09:26,514 --> 00:09:28,994
Mind your manners, Lu.

211
00:09:30,464 --> 00:09:32,514
I... uh... S-Sorry!

212
00:09:32,514 --> 00:09:36,854
I mean, why are y-you here, Phi?

213
00:09:36,854 --> 00:09:40,304
I was training outside today
 and I got back late.

214
00:09:40,304 --> 00:09:43,574
Relie said the bath was still open.

215
00:09:46,514 --> 00:09:49,034
<i>Her again...</i>

216
00:09:50,034 --> 00:09:52,984
Well, I-I'll be getting out, then.

217
00:09:52,984 --> 00:09:53,704
Why?

218
00:09:54,624 --> 00:09:59,474
Well, I'm sure you don't want
 to be here with a boy.

219
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:03,864
I wouldn't get into a bath
 a boy I didn't like was in.

220
00:10:03,864 --> 00:10:06,174
That's not what I'mâ

221
00:10:07,364 --> 00:10:10,984
It's been a while since we
 were last in a bath together.

222
00:10:10,984 --> 00:10:12,934
Brings back memories, doesn't it?

223
00:10:18,774 --> 00:10:20,694
<i>No! I can't go any further!</i>

224
00:10:27,254 --> 00:10:28,694
She's asleep!

225
00:10:30,324 --> 00:10:34,054
H-Hey! You can't fall asleep in the bath, Philuâ

226
00:10:35,844 --> 00:10:37,304
Th-This is bad!

227
00:10:37,304 --> 00:10:39,344
What's wrong, Lu?

228
00:10:39,344 --> 00:10:40,304
I-It's nothing.

229
00:10:40,304 --> 00:10:44,004
Anyway, you shouldn't 
fall asleep in the bath, Phi.

230
00:10:44,004 --> 00:10:44,714
Huh?

231
00:10:44,714 --> 00:10:46,734
You're right. Thanks.

232
00:10:47,394 --> 00:10:48,684
Say, Phi...

233
00:10:49,734 --> 00:10:50,594
What?

234
00:10:50,594 --> 00:10:53,704
Didn't you have a scar on your back?

235
00:10:53,704 --> 00:10:56,154
A small one going diagonally along here.

236
00:10:56,154 --> 00:10:57,624
Maybe.

237
00:10:57,624 --> 00:10:59,354
I don't really remember.

238
00:11:00,504 --> 00:11:04,914
<i>It wasn't a very deep scar,
 but I'm sure it was there.</i>

239
00:11:05,544 --> 00:11:08,614
Be careful tomorrow, Lu.

240
00:11:09,614 --> 00:11:11,614
You're going to the ruins, right?

241
00:11:11,614 --> 00:11:15,264
I can't go this time either, because of orders.

242
00:11:15,884 --> 00:11:20,004
I wanted to go, but Relie said I can't.

243
00:11:20,004 --> 00:11:21,564
R-Right.

244
00:11:21,564 --> 00:11:24,714
Don't worry. I'll come back.

245
00:11:24,714 --> 00:11:27,694
Uh, are you still not getting out?

246
00:11:27,694 --> 00:11:31,214
I've already stayed a bit too long.

247
00:11:35,354 --> 00:11:37,514
Are you okay, Lu?

248
00:11:41,504 --> 00:11:43,024
I see you're all here.

249
00:11:43,024 --> 00:11:49,154
Before you set off, there was a last minute change of plans regarding today's ruins investigation.

250
00:11:49,154 --> 00:11:51,294
Please step forward, Lord Balzeride.

251
00:11:54,374 --> 00:11:56,914
What's going on? Why's he here?

252
00:11:57,374 --> 00:12:01,794
Let me introduce this mission's specialâ

253
00:12:01,794 --> 00:12:03,694
Allow me to introduce myself.

254
00:12:03,694 --> 00:12:06,924
There's no need for an instructor
 to bother with such explanations.

255
00:12:06,924 --> 00:12:10,004
My name is Balzeride Kreutzer.

256
00:12:10,004 --> 00:12:17,454
I've offered my services to assist in this mission
 to exterminate Abysses and investigate the ruins.

257
00:12:19,684 --> 00:12:22,674
What is the meaning of this, Instructor?

258
00:12:22,674 --> 00:12:23,654
Wellâ

259
00:12:23,654 --> 00:12:25,184
What's the problem?

260
00:12:25,184 --> 00:12:30,564
Is there a some reason an outsider can't participate in this important mission, Your Highness?

261
00:12:31,074 --> 00:12:36,164
Don't worry. I have no intention of hindering or arguing with the purpose of the mission.

262
00:12:36,164 --> 00:12:38,924
My intentions are pure.

263
00:12:38,924 --> 00:12:41,454
I thought you'd be happy about it.

264
00:12:41,454 --> 00:12:46,234
As the man who took third place
 in the Royal Capitol Tournament,

265
00:12:46,234 --> 00:12:49,844
I'm volunteering to be the shield
 for a group of frail maidens.

266
00:12:49,844 --> 00:12:51,044
We don't need your help!

267
00:12:51,044 --> 00:12:51,984
Furthermore,

268
00:12:52,874 --> 00:12:56,734
the girl who is to be my wife
 happens to be among you.

269
00:12:56,734 --> 00:13:01,014
I can't let anything happen to her
 during this dangerous mission.

270
00:13:02,354 --> 00:13:08,054
And so, Lord Balzeride will only be assisting
 with the extermination of Abysses.

271
00:13:08,674 --> 00:13:10,114
Understood?

272
00:13:10,114 --> 00:13:11,014
Yes, ma'am!

273
00:13:23,814 --> 00:13:25,774
Target confirmed.

274
00:13:25,774 --> 00:13:27,884
Everyone, prepare for battle.

275
00:13:29,384 --> 00:13:31,304
So these are the ruins.

276
00:13:31,884 --> 00:13:34,054
I'll go down first.

277
00:13:35,014 --> 00:13:36,214
Wait, Krulcifer!

278
00:13:36,214 --> 00:13:37,384
Don't rush ahead alone!

279
00:13:37,384 --> 00:13:40,394
I'll be fine. Please let me head in.

280
00:13:40,394 --> 00:13:41,894
Why is she in such a hurry?

281
00:13:45,214 --> 00:13:49,904
An attitude befitting one who is to be my wife.

282
00:13:51,434 --> 00:13:54,034
Be on your guard, everyone. Something's approaching.

283
00:13:54,034 --> 00:13:55,154
What?!

284
00:13:55,154 --> 00:13:57,404
Enemy detected on radar.

285
00:13:57,404 --> 00:13:58,424
It's an Abyss.

286
00:14:04,924 --> 00:14:06,044
That's a...

287
00:14:06,294 --> 00:14:07,294
Diablos?!

288
00:14:08,544 --> 00:14:09,754
A Diablos?

289
00:14:09,754 --> 00:14:13,804
Those are feared as being powerful enough 
to destroy a small city alone.

290
00:14:13,804 --> 00:14:16,424
Yes. It's a pretty tough opponent.

291
00:14:19,344 --> 00:14:19,934
Noct!

292
00:14:26,754 --> 00:14:27,394
Lux!

293
00:14:27,394 --> 00:14:28,774
Get away from it!

294
00:14:32,484 --> 00:14:35,324
It's going to break my sword.

295
00:14:44,734 --> 00:14:45,414
It's fast!

296
00:14:46,294 --> 00:14:47,294
Shalice!

297
00:14:51,584 --> 00:14:53,424
It's way too fast to hit!

298
00:15:01,394 --> 00:15:04,634
That's the Divine Raiment, Wise Blood.

299
00:15:07,224 --> 00:15:10,084
You're making such a big fuss over one Abyss.

300
00:15:10,644 --> 00:15:13,984
Compared to a Ragnarok, this is a joke.

301
00:15:21,164 --> 00:15:24,414
Is that the power of his Divine Raiment Machine Dragon?

302
00:15:24,414 --> 00:15:28,634
How about it, fallen prince?
 Won't you have a contest with me?

303
00:15:29,294 --> 00:15:32,754
Whoever manages to 
take down that Abyss wins.

304
00:15:32,754 --> 00:15:36,424
If you win, I'll withdraw from our duel.

305
00:15:37,174 --> 00:15:39,514
Stop fooling around, Balzeride!

306
00:15:39,514 --> 00:15:43,834
If you continue interfering with the mission,
 I'll have to beat you down!

307
00:15:43,834 --> 00:15:46,934
Do you doubt yourself, Lux Arcadia?

308
00:15:48,384 --> 00:15:49,674
How can you...

309
00:15:49,674 --> 00:15:52,524
Can you please stop these foolish games?

310
00:15:57,904 --> 00:16:01,254
Such a cold thing to say, future wife of mine.

311
00:16:01,254 --> 00:16:04,454
I'll be getting rid of this enemy before you.

312
00:16:04,824 --> 00:16:06,824
I hope that's not a problem.

313
00:16:06,824 --> 00:16:08,074
Krulcifer!

314
00:16:08,074 --> 00:16:09,834
Wait! Don't do anything rash!

315
00:16:10,204 --> 00:16:11,524
Wise Blood!

316
00:16:12,234 --> 00:16:13,834
<i>I'll take you down this time!</i>

317
00:16:19,504 --> 00:16:20,514
Krulcifer...

318
00:16:26,974 --> 00:16:28,104
Watch out!

319
00:16:28,104 --> 00:16:28,854
Lux!

320
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:48,744
I win this round, fallen prince!

321
00:16:48,744 --> 00:16:51,624
Like I expected, no one could beat me to it.

322
00:16:52,594 --> 00:16:54,034
Something's wrong.

323
00:16:54,034 --> 00:16:56,334
Why can't I use Wise Blood?

324
00:16:59,054 --> 00:17:00,254
Don't let your guard down!

325
00:17:04,934 --> 00:17:05,954
Oh, no!

326
00:17:05,954 --> 00:17:07,614
Everyone, prepare for the shock wave!

327
00:17:07,614 --> 00:17:09,434
Full power to your defensive barriers!

328
00:17:24,584 --> 00:17:27,104
Crap! Fafnir is out of control!

329
00:17:28,544 --> 00:17:31,084
What's going on? Why?

330
00:17:37,714 --> 00:17:39,964
What's happening? The ruins are glowing!

331
00:18:04,634 --> 00:18:05,634
Are you all right?!

332
00:18:06,594 --> 00:18:08,864
You're a top class pilot.
 How did you lose control?

333
00:18:15,114 --> 00:18:18,404
And what in the world is this?

334
00:18:20,744 --> 00:18:21,754
Wait, did you...

335
00:18:21,754 --> 00:18:25,904
I just tried a new technique.

336
00:18:26,904 --> 00:18:32,164
With only the normal abilities,
 I'll just end up with regrets again.

337
00:18:41,024 --> 00:18:42,264
Guys?!

338
00:18:48,784 --> 00:18:51,234
Where am I?

339
00:18:51,924 --> 00:18:53,384
We're probably inside the ruins.

340
00:18:54,334 --> 00:18:57,154
Keep your voice down.

341
00:18:57,154 --> 00:19:00,174
It's dangerous while we don't
 understand the situation we're in.

342
00:19:00,174 --> 00:19:01,934
Right. I'm sorry.

343
00:19:01,934 --> 00:19:04,464
So, what happened?

344
00:19:04,464 --> 00:19:06,494
I remember the Abyss exploding, but...

345
00:19:07,114 --> 00:19:10,684
It seems the explosion drew us into the ruins.

346
00:19:11,224 --> 00:19:14,944
I didn't suffer any injuries
 because you protected me.

347
00:19:14,944 --> 00:19:15,894
Thank you.

348
00:19:15,894 --> 00:19:18,314
Oh, of course. I'm just glad you're not hurt.

349
00:19:18,854 --> 00:19:28,164
Now, we were supposed to head for the altar at the center once we successfully enter the ruins.

350
00:19:28,164 --> 00:19:30,324
We should be able to meet up 
with the others there.

351
00:19:30,324 --> 00:19:31,594
Really?

352
00:19:31,594 --> 00:19:33,144
Come on. Let's go.

353
00:19:33,664 --> 00:19:35,144
Uh, okay.

354
00:19:43,124 --> 00:19:44,964
It looks like it's going to rain.

355
00:19:44,964 --> 00:19:46,154
Rain?

356
00:19:46,154 --> 00:19:48,184
You think it rains in here?

357
00:19:48,184 --> 00:19:49,454
It would seem so.

358
00:19:50,074 --> 00:19:52,744
Though no one knows how that occurs.

359
00:19:55,474 --> 00:19:56,424
Careful!

360
00:19:57,284 --> 00:19:59,854
You're still drained from the fight.

361
00:19:59,854 --> 00:20:01,894
Let's take it easy for a bit.

362
00:20:01,894 --> 00:20:02,954
I'm fine.

363
00:20:02,954 --> 00:20:03,984
You sure?

364
00:20:04,844 --> 00:20:09,074
I can't stop here.

365
00:20:09,074 --> 00:20:11,284
This is one of my few precious opportunities.

366
00:20:21,224 --> 00:20:24,414
All right. Lean on my shoulder, then.

367
00:20:44,274 --> 00:20:46,394
Say, Krulcifer...

368
00:20:46,394 --> 00:20:48,114
What is it?

369
00:20:48,114 --> 00:20:51,654
Why are you looking for the Black Hero?

370
00:20:52,454 --> 00:20:56,184
Normally, no matter how much
 they push themselves,

371
00:20:56,184 --> 00:20:59,014
there's a limit to how long a person can pilot a Mechanical Dragon.

372
00:20:59,014 --> 00:21:02,414
But the Black Hero doesn't have that limit.

373
00:21:03,404 --> 00:21:06,404
At least, I'm looking for him,
 hoping to find that to be true.

374
00:21:06,404 --> 00:21:08,624
Hoping to find a person like myself.

375
00:21:14,534 --> 00:21:17,684
We're the first to arrive, from the looks of it.

376
00:21:17,684 --> 00:21:19,784
What? This is the altar?

377
00:21:31,754 --> 00:21:33,824
This should be the key.

378
00:21:34,214 --> 00:21:36,044
I guess I should blow it here.

379
00:21:41,064 --> 00:21:43,514
Presence of key acknowledged.

380
00:21:43,514 --> 00:21:45,964
Unlocking special code.

381
00:21:45,964 --> 00:21:46,924
Key?!

382
00:21:47,614 --> 00:21:48,774
Yes.

383
00:21:48,774 --> 00:21:51,354
I'm not from this world.

384
00:21:51,354 --> 00:21:52,264
What?!

385
00:21:54,624 --> 00:21:58,244
I'm a survivor from the ruins.

